    "createdAt": "2026-11-04T00:00:00.000Z",
    "notes": "A post effect draws passes over the finished screen. The first pass copies the screen (minecraft:main) into the target msm_examples:swap through the vanilla copy shader with a warm tint (ColorModulate multiplies red, green, blue and alpha); the second copies it back. The game uses post effects it knows by name, such as minecraft:creeper while spectating a creeper: name a project effect after one to replace it. MSM does not check shader files, so look at the result in game.",
